# Targets chezmoi should DELETE from $HOME. chezmoi does not remove a file just
# because the source stopped managing it, so a renamed unit would otherwise sit
# in ~/.config/systemd/user/ forever -- still enabled, still pulled into
# graphical-session.target, and now pointing at an ExecStart that no longer
# exists on a machine that never had the shims.
#
# swww.service -> awww.service (2026-08-31): the unit was renamed when the
# /usr/local/bin/swww* shims were dropped in favour of waypaper's native awww
# backend. Disable it before the rename lands, or the stale
# graphical-session.target.wants/ symlink outlives the file it points at.
.config/systemd/user/swww.service

# hyprland.conf -> hyprland.lua (2026-09-16): DMS 1.6 only writes Lua fragments.
# dms-binds re-pointed the DMS session's launcher keys with `hyprctl keyword`,
# which a Lua config refuses; hyprland.lua does it natively now. The unit is only
# ever runtime-enabled by hyprland-dms, so no .wants/ symlink outlives it.
# hyprland.conf and workspaces.conf are deliberately NOT removed here: Hyprland
# ignores them while hyprland.lua exists. They are NOT a working fallback on
# their own, though -- the scripts now speak `hyprctl eval` -- so rolling back
# means reverting the commit, not renaming a file.
.config/systemd/user/dms-binds.service
.local/bin/dms-binds
